    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i've been trying out that box breathing thing (4 in, 4 hold, 4 out, 4 hold) to help with stress. can you explain what's actually happening in my body when i do that? like, how does it affect my nervous system or cortisol?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Box breathing, involving an inhale, hold, exhale, and hold, helps regulate your autonomic nervous system. This technique can activate your parasympathetic nervous system – the rest and digest part of your autonomic nervous system – which promotes relaxation. By maintaining a calm and controlled breathing pattern, it helps reduce the levels of the stress hormone cortisol, leading to a decrease in anxiety and stress. Practicing consistently can help improve your overall stress resilience.",
      "source": "target",
